@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il31-nouns`
IMPORT `il31-ito66-vintages`
IMPORT `ito-il03-nouns`
IMPORT `il31-ito121b-2025`

-- Tests for BACKLOG IL-31. Every expected value was worked out by hand from the Hebrew of the
-- Acts (read from the page images) or of the consolidation, and the arithmetic is written beside
-- each group, BEFORE the assertion was run. None was copied from an evaluation. A failing
-- assertion here is a finding about the source or the encoding, never a value to edit.
--
-- Two kinds of number appear, and each says which it is:
--   * figures the Acts print (2 1/2, 4 1/2, 3 1/2, 2, 1, 1/2 credit points; 13 years; 3%; 2%;
--     5,385,285; the commencement dates 1 January 2024 and 1 January 2025);
--   * 721,560, the s 121B(a) amount for 2024-2027 given by the consolidation's editorial note
--     (source line 4456). It is not law here: it is supplied as a scenario value, the way a
--     caller would supply the published figure.

§ `Tests`

-- ===========================================================================
-- PART A. Section 66(c)(4)-(6) before 2024.
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `A. Fixtures`

GIVEN b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A child in section 66(c)`
`a child born in tax year` b MEANS
    `A child in section 66(c)` WITH `tax year of birth` IS b

`the woman` MEANS `a woman, under paragraph (4)`
`the woman who married a widower` MEANS `a woman who married a widower, under paragraph (4A)`
`the man` MEANS `a man, under paragraph (5)`
`the man who married a widow` MEANS `a man who married a widow, under paragraph (6)`

§§ `A1. Which vintage governs which tax year`

-- SH 3184 s 3: ss 40 and 66 as worded in its s 1 commence on 1 January 2024; SH 3048 s 3(a) and (d)
-- agree (income produced from that day). Tax year 2024 is the first. SH 2972 s 1: income produced
-- from 1 January to 31 December 2022 only.
#ASSERT `the first tax year of the text of section 66(c)(4)-(6) that Acts SH 3048 and SH 3184 leave` EQUALS 2024
#ASSERT `the vintage of section 66(c)(4)-(6) that governs tax year` 2024 EQUALS `the text of Acts SH 3048 and SH 3184, from tax year 2024`
#ASSERT `the vintage of section 66(c)(4)-(6) that governs tax year` 2026 EQUALS `the text of Acts SH 3048 and SH 3184, from tax year 2024`
#ASSERT `the vintage of section 66(c)(4)-(6) that governs tax year` 2023 EQUALS `the base text, in tax year 2023`
#ASSERT `the vintage of section 66(c)(4)-(6) that governs tax year` 2022 EQUALS `the base text with the temporary provision of Act SH 2972, in tax year 2022`
#ASSERT `the vintage of section 66(c)(4)-(6) that governs tax year` 2021 EQUALS `a text before tax year 2022`
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 reads the Ordinance for income produced in tax year` 2022
#ASSERT NOT `Act SH 2972 reads the Ordinance for income produced in tax year` 2021
#ASSERT NOT `Act SH 2972 reads the Ordinance for income produced in tax year` 2023

§§ `A2. The credit points the Acts' text gives, by age in tax years (tax year 2024 and later)`

-- The woman, (4)(a): 0 -> 2 1/2; 1 and 2 -> 4 1/2; 3 -> 3 1/2; 4 and 5 -> 2 1/2; 6 to 17 -> 2;
-- 18 (the year of maturity) -> 1/2; otherwise none.
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)(a) — the credit points for a child of` 0 EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)(a) — the credit points for a child of` 1 EQUALS 4.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)(a) — the credit points for a child of` 2 EQUALS 4.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)(a) — the credit points for a child of` 3 EQUALS 3.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)(a) — the credit points for a child of` 4 EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)(a) — the credit points for a child of` 5 EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)(a) — the credit points for a child of` 6 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)(a) — the credit points for a child of` 17 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)(a) — the credit points for a child of` 18 EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)(a) — the credit points for a child of` 19 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)(a) — the credit points for a child of` (0 MINUS 1) EQUALS 0

-- The man, (5): 0 -> 2 1/2; 1 and 2 -> 4 1/2; 3 -> 3 1/2; 4 and 5 -> 2 1/2; 6 to 17 -> 1; (5) names
-- no point for the year of maturity, so 18 -> none.
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(5) — the credit points for a child of` 0 EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(5) — the credit points for a child of` 1 EQUALS 4.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(5) — the credit points for a child of` 2 EQUALS 4.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(5) — the credit points for a child of` 3 EQUALS 3.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(5) — the credit points for a child of` 4 EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(5) — the credit points for a child of` 5 EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(5) — the credit points for a child of` 6 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(5) — the credit points for a child of` 17 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(5) — the credit points for a child of` 18 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(5) — the credit points for a child of` 19 EQUALS 0

-- The four claimants take the column of paragraph (4) or (5) as their paragraph says.
#ASSERT `the credit points the paragraph gives` `the woman` `for a child of` 18 EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `the credit points the paragraph gives` `the woman who married a widower` `for a child of` 18 EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `the credit points the paragraph gives` `the man` `for a child of` 18 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points the paragraph gives` `the man who married a widow` `for a child of` 18 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points the paragraph gives` `the woman who married a widower` `for a child of` 7 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the credit points the paragraph gives` `the man who married a widow` `for a child of` 7 EQUALS 1

§§ `A3. The entry, by tax year and year of birth`

-- Tax year 2024: age = 2024 - year of birth.
--   born 2024 -> age 0;  born 2023 -> age 1;  born 2021 -> age 3;  born 2018 -> age 6;
--   born 2007 -> age 17;  born 2006 -> age 18.
-- The woman, then the man.
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2024) `in tax year` 2024 `, before any election under (4)(a1)` EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2023) `in tax year` 2024 `, before any election under (4)(a1)` EQUALS 4.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2021) `in tax year` 2024 `, before any election under (4)(a1)` EQUALS 3.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2018) `in tax year` 2024 `, before any election under (4)(a1)` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2007) `in tax year` 2024 `, before any election under (4)(a1)` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2006) `in tax year` 2024 `, before any election under (4)(a1)` EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the man` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2024) `in tax year` 2024 `, before any election under (4)(a1)` EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the man` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2023) `in tax year` 2024 `, before any election under (4)(a1)` EQUALS 4.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the man` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2018) `in tax year` 2024 `, before any election under (4)(a1)` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the man` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2006) `in tax year` 2024 `, before any election under (4)(a1)` EQUALS 0
-- Tax year 2025 and 2026 are the same text (the section's amendment list ends at SH 3184).
--   born 2025, tax year 2025 -> age 0;  born 2020, tax year 2026 -> age 6.
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2025) `in tax year` 2025 `, before any election under (4)(a1)` EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the man` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2020) `in tax year` 2026 `, before any election under (4)(a1)` EQUALS 1
-- The step-parents.  Born 2021, tax year 2024: age 3 -> 3 1/2 for each.
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the woman who married a widower` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2021) `in tax year` 2024 `, before any election under (4)(a1)` EQUALS 3.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the man who married a widow` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2021) `in tax year` 2024 `, before any election under (4)(a1)` EQUALS 3.5

§§ `A4. Before 2024: declined by name, whatever the claimant or the child`

#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2023) `in tax year` 2023 `, before any election under (4)(a1)`
        BECAUSE "the text of section 66(c)(4)-(6) in tax year 2023 needs a source: its text before Act SH 3048 (paragraphs (4), (5) and (6), and the definition of a toddler in section 40(b)(3)), and the 5783 Act tagged in the amendment list, none of which is deposited"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the man` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2010) `in tax year` 2023 `, before any election under (4)(a1)`
        BECAUSE "the text of section 66(c)(4)-(6) in tax year 2023 needs a source: its text before Act SH 3048 (paragraphs (4), (5) and (6), and the definition of a toddler in section 40(b)(3)), and the 5783 Act tagged in the amendment list, none of which is deposited"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2015) `in tax year` 2022 `, before any election under (4)(a1)`
        BECAUSE "the text of section 66(c)(4)-(6) in tax year 2022 needs a source: the base text on which Act SH 2972 only adds, which is not deposited"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the woman who married a widower` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2015) `in tax year` 2021 `, before any election under (4)(a1)`
        BECAUSE "the text of section 66(c)(4)-(6) before tax year 2022 needs a source: the amending Acts of those years are not deposited"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of` `the man who married a widow` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2015) `in tax year` 2000 `, before any election under (4)(a1)`
        BECAUSE "the text of section 66(c)(4)-(6) before tax year 2022 needs a source: the amending Acts of those years are not deposited"

§§ `A5. Tax year 2022: the further credit point Act SH 2972 gives`

-- Worked from SH 2972 s 1(2)(a)-(c): one further point, for each child who "in 2022 had not yet
-- completed thirteen years" and is not a toddler, to the woman ((4)(d)), the man ((5A)), and the
-- step-parents (through (4A) and (6)); none for a toddler; none outside 2022.
-- A child's age in 2022, counted in tax years, is 2022 minus the year of birth.
--   born 2015 -> age 7, born 2010 -> age 12 (both under 13); born 2008 -> age 14 (over);
--   born 2009 -> age 13: the readings part (fork A1).
`a toddler` MEANS TRUE
`not a toddler` MEANS FALSE

-- A child of age 7, not a toddler: one point to each of the four claimants, every reading.
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2015) `, toddler status` `not a toddler` `, in tax year` 2022 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the woman who married a widower` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2015) `, toddler status` `not a toddler` `, in tax year` 2022 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the man` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2015) `, toddler status` `not a toddler` `, in tax year` 2022 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the man who married a widow` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2015) `, toddler status` `not a toddler` `, in tax year` 2022 EQUALS 1
-- Born 2010 (age 12): in on both readings, and by default.
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2010) `, toddler status` `not a toddler` `, in tax year` 2022 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2010) `, toddler status` `not a toddler` `, in tax year` 2022 `, reading the age limit as` `the age is counted in tax years, so a child born in 2009 has completed thirteen years in 2022` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2010) `, toddler status` `not a toddler` `, in tax year` 2022 `, reading the age limit as` `the age is tested at the start of 2022, so a child born in 2009 has not completed thirteen years` EQUALS 1
-- Born 2008 (age 14): out on both readings, and by default.
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the man` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2008) `, toddler status` `not a toddler` `, in tax year` 2022 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the man` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2008) `, toddler status` `not a toddler` `, in tax year` 2022 `, reading the age limit as` `the age is counted in tax years, so a child born in 2009 has completed thirteen years in 2022` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the man` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2008) `, toddler status` `not a toddler` `, in tax year` 2022 `, reading the age limit as` `the age is tested at the start of 2022, so a child born in 2009 has not completed thirteen years` EQUALS 0
-- Born 2009 (age 13): (i) counted in tax years, out: 13 is not less than 13;
-- (ii) tested at the start of 2022, in: 13 is at most 13; by default the text does not decide.
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2009) `, toddler status` `not a toddler` `, in tax year` 2022 `, reading the age limit as` `the age is counted in tax years, so a child born in 2009 has completed thirteen years in 2022` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2009) `, toddler status` `not a toddler` `, in tax year` 2022 `, reading the age limit as` `the age is tested at the start of 2022, so a child born in 2009 has not completed thirteen years` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT REFUSED `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2009) `, toddler status` `not a toddler` `, in tax year` 2022
        BECAUSE "section 66(c)(4)(d), (5A) as Act SH 2972 gives them: the readings of the age limit of thirteen years part for a child born in 2009, and the text does not decide which day of 2022 the age is tested"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the man who married a widow` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2009) `, toddler status` `not a toddler` `, in tax year` 2022 `, reading the age limit as` `declined where the reading changes the answer`
        BECAUSE "section 66(c)(4)(d), (5A) as Act SH 2972 gives them: the readings of the age limit of thirteen years part for a child born in 2009, and the text does not decide which day of 2022 the age is tested"
-- A toddler gets nothing, and the question of the age limit is never reached (so no refusal),
-- even for a child born in 2009 under the default switch.
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2021) `, toddler status` `a toddler` `, in tax year` 2022 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2009) `, toddler status` `a toddler` `, in tax year` 2022 EQUALS 0
-- Outside 2022 the Act adds nothing (it covers 1 January to 31 December 2022); the year gate comes
-- before the age limit, so a child born in 2009 raises no refusal in 2023.
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2015) `, toddler status` `not a toddler` `, in tax year` 2021 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2015) `, toddler status` `not a toddler` `, in tax year` 2023 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Act SH 2972 — the further credit point of` `the woman` `for` (`a child born in tax year` 2009) `, toddler status` `not a toddler` `, in tax year` 2023 EQUALS 0
-- The switch names the default reading.
#ASSERT `section 66(c)(4)(d), (5A) — the reading this row takes for the age limit of thirteen years in 2022` EQUALS `declined where the reading changes the answer`

-- ===========================================================================
-- PART B. Section 121B in tax year 2025.
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `B. Fixtures`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`a salary of` n MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS TRUE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS TRUE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS TRUE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS FALSE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS 0

-- Income from personal exertion that is not s 2(1)/(2) income (a pension, say): excluded from the
-- capital-source definition by its paragraph (2).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`a pension of` n MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS TRUE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS FALSE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS TRUE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS FALSE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS 0

-- A dividend: not personal exertion, not s 2(1)/(2): capital-source income.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`a dividend of` n MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS FALSE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS FALSE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS FALSE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS FALSE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS 0

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`a capital gain of` n `, of which inflationary` m MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS FALSE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS FALSE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS FALSE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS FALSE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS m

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`rent taxed on the scale, of` n MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS FALSE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS FALSE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS TRUE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS FALSE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS 0

-- A sale of a right in a residential apartment.
GIVEN v IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      i IS A NUMBER
      x IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A sale of a right in real estate`
`a residential sale for` v `, betterment` b `, of which inflationary` i `, exempt` x MEANS
    `A sale of a right in real estate` WITH
        `betterment`                                                                    IS b
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 47 of the Real Estate Taxation Law` IS i
        `in a residential apartment`                                                    IS TRUE
        `sale value`                                                                    IS v
        `exempt from tax under any law`                                                 IS x

-- A sale of other land: the residential limb is never consulted.
GIVEN v IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      i IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A sale of a right in real estate`
`a sale of other land for` v `, betterment` b `, of which inflationary` i MEANS
    `A sale of a right in real estate` WITH
        `betterment`                                                                    IS b
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 47 of the Real Estate Taxation Law` IS i
        `in a residential apartment`                                                    IS FALSE
        `sale value`                                                                    IS v
        `exempt from tax under any law`                                                 IS FALSE

GIVEN y     IS A NUMBER
      items IS A LIST OF `An item of income`
      sales IS A LIST OF `A sale of a right in real estate`
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year`
`an individual in tax year` y `, with income` items `and sales` sales MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                       IS y
        `date of birth`                  IS YMD 1980 6 15
        `items of income`                IS items
        `sales of rights in real estate` IS sales

-- The scenario amount: 721,560 is the consolidation's editorial figure for 2024-2027, NOT law here.
`the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` MEANS 721_560

GIVEN y     IS A NUMBER
      items IS A LIST OF `An item of income`
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year`
`in tax year` y `, income` items MEANS
    `an individual in tax year` y `, with income` items `and sales` (EMPTY)

§§ `B1. The date and the year the Act reaches`

-- SH 3342 s 3(b): (a1) applies to income produced or received on 1 January 2025 or later.
#ASSERT NOT `s 121B(a1) applies to income produced or received on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2024)
#ASSERT `s 121B(a1) applies to income produced or received on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2025)
#ASSERT `s 121B(a1) applies to income produced or received on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2025)
#ASSERT `the tax year in which Act SH 3342 commenced` EQUALS 2025

§§ `B2. The residential-apartment threshold`

-- SH 3342 s 1(2)(ה)(2): 5,385,285 shekels. Nothing adjusts it in 2025 (the base index is that of
-- 15 January 2027).
#ASSERT `SH 3342 text — the residential-apartment sale value in section 121B(e) for tax year` 2025 EQUALS 5_385_285
#ASSERT REFUSED `SH 3342 text — the residential-apartment sale value in section 121B(e) for tax year` 2024
        BECAUSE "section 121B for a tax year before 2025 needs a source: its text before Act SH 3342 (amendment 276), which the Act amends by words and which is not deposited, and the Act does not say to which tax year income produced earlier but received from 1 January 2025 belongs"
#ASSERT REFUSED `SH 3342 text — the residential-apartment sale value in section 121B(e) for tax year` 2026
        BECAUSE "section 121B from tax year 2026 is answered by row IL-03, not by the tax year 2025 vintage of row IL-31"

§§ `B3. The capital-source definition`

-- (e): taxable income from a capital source = taxable income except (1) s 2(1)/(2) income and
-- (2) other personal-exertion income.
#ASSERT NOT `SH 3342 text — from a capital source` (`a salary of` 100)
#ASSERT NOT `SH 3342 text — from a capital source` (`a pension of` 100)
#ASSERT `SH 3342 text — from a capital source` (`a dividend of` 100)
#ASSERT `SH 3342 text — from a capital source` (`a capital gain of` 100 `, of which inflationary` 10)
#ASSERT `SH 3342 text — from a capital source` (`rent taxed on the scale, of` 100)

§§ `B4. (a) and (a1): the two charges`

-- Amount A = 721,560.
-- Salary 1,000,000: taxable 1,000,000, capital-source 0.
--   (a)  3% x (1,000,000 - 721,560 = 278,440) = 8,353.2     (278,440 x 3 = 835,320; / 100)
--   (a1) capital 0 is not above A: 0
--   total 8,353.2
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2025 `, income` (LIST `a salary of` 1_000_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 8_353.2
-- Dividend 1,000,000: taxable 1,000,000, capital-source 1,000,000.
--   (a) 8,353.2;  (a1) 2% x 278,440 = 5,568.8 (278,440 x 2 = 556,880; / 100);  total 13,922
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2025 `, income` (LIST `a dividend of` 1_000_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 13_922
-- Salary 800,000 and dividend 300,000: taxable 1,100,000; capital-source 300,000 (not above A).
--   (a)  3% x (1,100,000 - 721,560 = 378,440) = 11,353.2   (378,440 x 3 = 1,135,320; / 100)
--   (a1) 0;  total 11,353.2
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2025 `, income` (LIST `a salary of` 800_000, `a dividend of` 300_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 11_353.2
-- Salary 100,000 and dividend 800,000: taxable 900,000; capital-source 800,000.
--   (a)  3% x (900,000 - 721,560 = 178,440) = 5,353.2      (178,440 x 3 = 535,320; / 100)
--   (a1) 2% x (800,000 - 721,560 = 78,440)  = 1,568.8      (78,440 x 2 = 156,880; / 100)
--   total 6,922
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2025 `, income` (LIST `a salary of` 100_000, `a dividend of` 800_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 6_922
-- A pension is personal exertion that is not s 2(1)/(2) income: not capital-source.
-- Pension 1,000,000: (a) 8,353.2; (a1) 0.
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2025 `, income` (LIST `a pension of` 1_000_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 8_353.2
-- Rent taxed on the scale 1,000,000 is capital-source: 13,922 as for a dividend.
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2025 `, income` (LIST `rent taxed on the scale, of` 1_000_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 13_922

-- Dividend 900,000 (taxable 900,000, capital-source 900,000):
--   (a) 3% x 178,440 = 5,353.2;  (a1) 2% x 178,440 = 3,568.8;  total 8,922.
-- (Worked here by hand; it is also the figure the independent tester of row IL-03 expected for
-- tax year 2025, `tests-independent.l4` line 371, which row IL-03 refuses.)
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2025 `, income` (LIST `a dividend of` 900_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 8_922

§§ `B5. Both sides of the threshold (fork F14: exceeds is strict)`

-- Salary exactly A: not above; 0.  Salary A + 1: 3% x 1 = 0.03.
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2025 `, income` (LIST `a salary of` 721_560)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 0
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2025 `, income` (LIST `a salary of` 721_561)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 0.03
-- Dividend exactly A: 0.  Dividend A + 1: (a) 0.03 + (a1) 2% x 1 = 0.02 = 0.05.
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2025 `, income` (LIST `a dividend of` 721_560)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 0
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2025 `, income` (LIST `a dividend of` 721_561)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 0.05
-- No income: 0.
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2025 `, income` (EMPTY)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 0

§§ `B6. The inflationary amount of s 88 is excluded`

-- Capital gain 900,000, of which inflationary 200,000: taxable 700,000, below A: 0.
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2025 `, income` (LIST `a capital gain of` 900_000 `, of which inflationary` 200_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 0
-- Capital gain 1,000,000, of which inflationary 100,000: taxable 900,000, capital-source 900,000.
--   (a)  3% x 178,440 = 5,353.2;  (a1) 2% x 178,440 = 3,568.8 (178,440 x 2 = 356,880; / 100);
--   total 8,922
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2025 `, income` (LIST `a capital gain of` 1_000_000 `, of which inflationary` 100_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 8_922

§§ `B7. Betterment on a sale of real estate (the residential limb)`

-- Residential, sale value 5,385,286 (above 5,385,285), not exempt, betterment 2,000,000 of which
-- the s 47 inflationary amount is 300,000: counts, net: 1,700,000; capital-source.
--   (a)  3% x (1,700,000 - 721,560 = 978,440) = 29,353.2   (978,440 x 3 = 2,935,320; / 100)
--   (a1) 2% x 978,440 = 19,568.8                            (978,440 x 2 = 1,956,880; / 100)
--   total 48,922
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`an individual in tax year` 2025 `, with income` (EMPTY) `and sales` (LIST `a residential sale for` 5_385_286 `, betterment` 2_000_000 `, of which inflationary` 300_000 `, exempt` FALSE)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 48_922
-- Sale value exactly 5,385,285: not above, the betterment does not count: 0, its inflationary
-- amount included (fork F9).
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`an individual in tax year` 2025 `, with income` (EMPTY) `and sales` (LIST `a residential sale for` 5_385_285 `, betterment` 2_000_000 `, of which inflationary` 300_000 `, exempt` FALSE)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 0
-- Above the threshold but exempt from tax under any law: does not count: 0.
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`an individual in tax year` 2025 `, with income` (EMPTY) `and sales` (LIST `a residential sale for` 9_000_000 `, betterment` 2_000_000 `, of which inflationary` 300_000 `, exempt` TRUE)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 0
-- Other land: the residential limb is not consulted, so a small sale value still counts.
--   Betterment 2,000,000 less 300,000 = 1,700,000: 48,922 as above.
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`an individual in tax year` 2025 `, with income` (EMPTY) `and sales` (LIST `a sale of other land for` 1_000_000 `, betterment` 2_000_000 `, of which inflationary` 300_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 48_922
-- Salary 500,000 and other land (betterment 400,000, inflationary 100,000 -> 300,000 counted):
-- taxable 800,000; capital-source 300,000.
--   (a) 3% x (800,000 - 721,560 = 78,440) = 2,353.2;  (a1) 0;  total 2,353.2
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`an individual in tax year` 2025 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 500_000) `and sales` (LIST `a sale of other land for` 1_000_000 `, betterment` 400_000 `, of which inflationary` 100_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 2_353.2

-- Salary 600,000 and a residential sale (betterment 200,000, no s 47 inflationary amount, sale
-- value 5,385,286, not exempt): the sale counts; taxable 800,000; capital-source 200,000 (below A).
--   (a) 3% x (800,000 - 721,560 = 78,440) = 2,353.2;  (a1) 0;  total 2,353.2
-- (The same case as the IL-03 independent tester's line 384, which row IL-03 refuses for 2025.)
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`an individual in tax year` 2025 `, with income` (LIST `a salary of` 600_000) `and sales` (LIST `a residential sale for` 5_385_286 `, betterment` 200_000 `, of which inflationary` 0 `, exempt` FALSE)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS RIGHT 2_353.2

§§ `B8. Facts that cannot be right are rejected, not answered`

#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2025 `, income` (LIST `a salary of` (0 MINUS 1))) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS LEFT `an amount of income is negative`
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2025 `, income` (LIST `a capital gain of` 900_000 `, of which inflationary` (0 MINUS 1))) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS LEFT `an inflationary amount is negative`
#ASSERT `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`an individual in tax year` 2025 `, with income` (EMPTY) `and sales` (LIST `a sale of other land for` 1_000_000 `, betterment` (0 MINUS 1) `, of which inflationary` 0)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027` EQUALS LEFT `a betterment or a sale value is negative`

§§ `B9. (b): section 91(d) on advance payments`

-- SH 3342 s 1(2)(ד): (b) now names (a) and (a1); section 91(d) does not apply to either.
#ASSERT NOT `SH 3342 text — s 121B(b) — section 91(d) on advance payments applies to income chargeable to additional tax under (a) or (a1)`

§§ `B10. Every other tax year is declined by name`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2024 `, income` (LIST `a salary of` 1_000_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027`
        BECAUSE "section 121B for a tax year before 2025 needs a source: its text before Act SH 3342 (amendment 276), which the Act amends by words and which is not deposited, and the Act does not say to which tax year income produced earlier but received from 1 January 2025 belongs"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2023 `, income` (LIST `a dividend of` 1_000_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027`
        BECAUSE "section 121B for a tax year before 2025 needs a source: its text before Act SH 3342 (amendment 276), which the Act amends by words and which is not deposited, and the Act does not say to which tax year income produced earlier but received from 1 January 2025 belongs"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the additional tax under section 121B in tax year 2025 for` (`in tax year` 2026 `, income` (LIST `a salary of` 1_000_000)) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount the editorial note gives for 2024-2027`
        BECAUSE "section 121B from tax year 2026 is answered by row IL-03, not by the tax year 2025 vintage of row IL-31"
